# =============================================================================
# .dockerignore — KI Translator KMU
# =============================================================================
# Excludes files that should never enter the Docker build context.
# A tight .dockerignore means faster builds (less data sent to the daemon)
# and no risk of accidentally leaking secrets into image layers.
# =============================================================================

# --- Version control & editor artifacts ---
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
*.swo

# --- Local environment files (secrets must never enter the image) ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example        # keep the example as documentation reference

# --- Next.js build artifacts (rebuilt inside Docker, not copied in) ---
.next
out

# --- Dependency directories (reinstalled fresh in the deps stage) ---
node_modules
.pnpm-store

# --- Development & test artifacts ---
coverage
*.test.ts
*.test.tsx
*.spec.ts
*.spec.tsx
__tests__
__mocks__

# --- Documentation (not needed at runtime) ---
README.md
CLAUDE.md
docs

# --- Docker files themselves (no need to nest Docker-in-Docker) ---
Dockerfile*
docker-compose*
.dockerignore

# --- OS artifacts ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Misc ---
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.turbo
